  "title": "Network of autoscopic hallucinations elicited by intracerebral stimulation of periventricular nodular heterotopia: SEEG during 43 Hz and single-pulse stimulation (1 patient)",
  "description": "Stereo-EEG recordings from a single drug-resistant epilepsy patient with a right posterior temporal periventricular nodular heterotopia (PVNH). 43 Hz electrical stimulation of the PVNH elicited autoscopic hallucinations, and single-pulse electrical stimulation was used to map effective connectivity. The dataset supports a multi-modal connectivity analysis of the network involving the PVNH, occipital and temporal neocortex, fusiform gyrus and parietal cortex. It is provided in iEEG-BIDS format with contact coordinates and a defaced T1 image.",
  "methods_description": "SEEG was recorded at 4096 Hz with a 128-channel XLTek Quantum system from depth electrodes. Bipolar stimulation was delivered with a Guideline 4000LP+ stimulator. High-frequency stimulation used 43.3 Hz biphasic alternating-polarity 1 ms pulses for 5 s at 0.25-3 mA. Single-pulse stimulation used 20 pulses per trial, a 15 s inter-stimulus interval and 3 ms pulses at 0.25-5 mA.",
